Real, verified unified diff (git diff in target/gecko-src/gecko-dev,
branch central-work @ 5836a062726f715fda621338a17b51aff30d0a8c) against
the upstream file browser/base/content/browser-init.js — apply with
`git apply` or `patch -p1` from the checkout root.

Implements pyxis-scheme-and-kiosk-plan.md Part B1 point 3 (WM_CLASS/
title stamping for Evo's create/claim contract). Adapts the real,
already-shipping `taskbartab` attribute-stamping block immediately
above the inserted code (same function, onBeforeInitialXULLayout()) -
see that block for the precedent this copies the shape of. Verified
against the real tree that onBeforeInitialXULLayout() genuinely runs
before AppWindow::SyncAttributesToWidget() reads windowclass/windowname:
it's wired to the MozBeforeInitialXULLayout DOM event
(browser/base/content/browser-main.js), which
dom/prototype/PrototypeDocumentContentSink.cpp dispatches synchronously
immediately before calling StartLayout() (line ~656-666), and
StartLayout() is what eventually calls AppWindow::BeforeStartLayout()
(via Document::SetMayStartLayout(), dom/base/Document.cpp:9821-9829).

UPDATE (2026-07-08): added a PYXIS block in delayed startup that sets
window.fullScreen for a PYXIS_DISPLAY_MODE=fullscreen pyxis window (the
shell). NOTE: this is belt-and-suspenders only -- verified live it does NOT
by itself fullscreen the shell (the chromeless/popup-like pyxis window
ignores it). The shell is actually made chromeless+fullscreen by (a) --kiosk
on its vela launch (native gtk_window_set_decorated(false)) and (b) Evo
initiating the fullscreen compositor-side (evo/src/shell/xdg.rs ack_configure
SHELL_APP_ID). Kept because it's harmless and documents intent. See
evo-firefox-decoration-arch.

UPDATE (2026-09-25): added a permanent `PYXIS-DIAG chrome-late:` block to
delayed startup, logging the app window's settled chrome state (toolbar.visible,
#nav-bar height, chromehidden) 5s after load. This is the regression guard for
the "second and subsequent launches come up with full Firefox chrome" bug --
see the SessionStore.sys.mjs patch in this series for the root cause. It is
permanent, not a temporary probe: that window is born chromeless and has its
chrome flags rewritten ~2s later, so every check made at window open reports a
correct window, and there is no other way to observe the settled state (serial
console only; QMP screendump reports "no surface" on Evo's GL scanout).
Asserted by scripts/serial-tests/kiosk-relaunch.txt.
UPDATE (2026-09-27): the shell's overlay window. A window opened with the
`pyxisOverlay` key (openPyxisAppWindow's `overlay` option, in the
BrowserContentHandler patch) gets the app id `<appId>-overlay` instead of
`<appId>`, a `pyxisoverlay` root attribute, and a USER sheet that makes its
chrome paint nothing (user !important outranks any !important background in
browser chrome's author sheets). Evo stacks that app id above app windows and
passes clicks through it except where Bloom reports it draws
(evo/src/shell/overlay.rs). The window is only transparent if the profile
also sets mozilla.widget.use-argb-visuals (an alpha visual, which Gecko
decides at widget creation) and browser.tabs.allow_transparent_browser;
geckoOS-boot sets both for the shell. Verified on device 2026-09-27: the
desktop shows through the overlay, and the overlay's drawing sits above a
maximized app.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser-init.js b/browser/base/content/browser-init.js
index c32b781be079..bff5d7d7167d 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser-init.js
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser-init.js
@@ -101,6 +101,23 @@ var gBrowserInit = {
       );
       toolbarMenubar.setAttribute("data-l10n-attrs", "toolbarname");
     }
+    // PYXIS-DIAG (temporary, 2026-08-17): the decisive probe for alpha2 #10.
+    // This logs unconditionally -- BEFORE the `window.arguments[1]` guard --
+    // so a window that arrives with no arguments at all is distinguishable
+    // from one whose arguments are present but the wrong shape. Those two
+    // cases have completely different fixes. Remove once #10 is closed.
+    try {
+      let a = window.arguments;
+      console.error(
+        `PYXIS-DIAG browser-init: arguments=${a ? a.length : "none"} ` +
+          `[1]=${a && a[1] ? String(a[1]) : "undefined"} ` +
+          `isBag=${!!(a && a[1] && a[1] instanceof Ci.nsIWritablePropertyBag2)} ` +
+          `hasPyxisApp=${!!(a && a[1] && a[1] instanceof Ci.nsIWritablePropertyBag2 && a[1].hasKey("pyxisApp"))}`
+      );
+    } catch (e) {
+      console.error(`PYXIS-DIAG browser-init: probe threw: ${e}`);
+    }
+
     // If opening a Taskbar Tab window, add an attribute to the top-level element
     // to inform window styling.
     if (window.arguments && window.arguments[1]) {
@@ -114,6 +131,73 @@ var gBrowserInit = {
           extraOptions.getPropertyAsAString("taskbartab")
         );
       }
+
+      // PYXIS: same shape as the taskbartab block directly above (real
+      // precedent this is adapted from) - openPyxisAppWindow() in
+      // BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs stamps a "pyxisApp" key onto the
+      // same extraOptions property bag instead of "taskbartab". Setting
+      // `windowclass`/`windowname` here, BEFORE this window's initial XUL
+      // layout, is what makes AppWindow::SyncAttributesToWidget()
+      // (xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp, called from BeforeStartLayout())
+      // pick them up and call nsWindow::SetWindowClass()
+      // (widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp), which is the real mechanism that stamps
+      // WM_CLASS (X11) / the xdg-toplevel app_id (Wayland,
+      // gdk_wayland_window_set_application_id via RefreshWindowClass()) -
+      // see that function for why this must happen before first paint,
+      // not after. `pyxisapp` (lowercase, matching the `taskbartab`
+      // attribute's all-lowercase convention - XML/HTML attribute names
+      // are case-insensitive so this is also just a style match) drives
+      // any pyxis-specific CSS keyed off it, mirroring
+      // panelUI-shared.css's `:root[taskbartab]` selector.
+      if (
+        extraOptions instanceof Ci.nsIWritablePropertyBag2 &&
+        extraOptions.hasKey("pyxisApp")
+      ) {
+        let appId = extraOptions.getPropertyAsAString("pyxisApp");
+        let root = window.document.documentElement;
+        root.setAttribute("pyxisapp", appId);
+        // "windowclass"/"windowname" are read by
+        // AppWindow::SyncAttributesToWidget() via plain
+        // GetAttribute(u"windowclass"_ns, ...) / GetAttribute(u"windowname"_ns,
+        // ...) calls (NOT interned nsGkAtoms, so no atom-table change was
+        // needed for this patch) - see that function in AppWindow.cpp.
+        // nsWindow::SetWindowClass() then splits `windowclass` into
+        // res_name/res_class (X11 XClassHint) and uses `windowclass`
+        // as-is for the Wayland app_id. Evo's two-step
+        // create/claim contract (evo/src/enhancements/echo_ipc.rs)
+        // correlates on this app_id, so it must exactly equal
+        // PYXIS_APP_ID with no transformation - unlike the generic
+        // xulWinType-derived path in SetWindowClass (which uppercases the
+        // first letter and replaces non-alphanumeric characters), passing
+        // `windowclass` directly bypasses that transform entirely.
+        // The shell's overlay window (openPyxisAppWindow's `overlay`
+        // option) gets its own app id, `<appId>-overlay`, which is how Evo
+        // knows to stack it above app windows and pass clicks through it
+        // (evo/src/shell/overlay.rs). It is transparent wherever its page
+        // draws nothing. Three things make it so: an alpha visual
+        // (`mozilla.widget.use-argb-visuals`, a user pref, set for the shell
+        // only), a transparent <browser> (`browser.tabs.allow_transparent_browser`),
+        // and the chrome below painting nothing at all. The last is a USER
+        // sheet because user !important outranks any !important background in
+        // browser chrome's own (author) sheets.
+        let windowClass = appId;
+        if (extraOptions.hasKey("pyxisOverlay")) {
+          windowClass = `${appId}-overlay`;
+          root.setAttribute("pyxisoverlay", "true");
+          window.windowUtils.loadSheetUsingURIString(
+            "data:text/css," +
+              encodeURIComponent(
+                ":root[pyxisoverlay], :root[pyxisoverlay] * {" +
+                  " background: transparent !important;" +
+                  " appearance: none !important;" +
+                  " box-shadow: none !important; }"
+              ),
+            window.windowUtils.USER_SHEET
+          );
+        }
+        root.setAttribute("windowclass", windowClass);
+        root.setAttribute("windowname", windowClass);
+      }
     }
 
     // Run menubar initialization first, to avoid CustomTitlebar code picking
@@ -524,6 +608,77 @@ var gBrowserInit = {
       }
     }
 
+    // PYXIS: the desktop shell (Bloom, PYXIS_DISPLAY_MODE=fullscreen) must
+    // open chromeless. Setting `window.fullScreen` HERE -- from the window's
+    // own delayed startup, exactly where/when kiosk mode does it above -- is
+    // what actually issues the Wayland xdg set_fullscreen. Doing it from the
+    // opener's `window.open(...).then(win => win.fullScreen = true)` callback
+    // (BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs's openPyxisAppWindow) runs BEFORE this
+    // window's widget is realized, so it was silently lost and the shell
+    // stayed a normal, GTK-decorated window. Real fullscreen is the only
+    // reliable way to drop GTK's own titlebar on Wayland (see the
+    // vela-gtk-titlebar-decoration analysis: MOZ_GTK_TITLEBAR_DECORATION only
+    // stops Firefox's CSD, not GTK's default decoration). Evo composites the
+    // shell's fullscreen NON-exclusively (evo/src/shell/xdg.rs's SHELL_APP_ID
+    // branch in fullscreen_request), so ordinary app windows still stack on
+    // top of it. Guarded by the `pyxisapp` attribute (set in the PYXIS block
+    // of onBeforeInitialXULLayout above) so only the real pyxis-app toplevel
+    // -- not some popup in the same process -- is affected.
+    try {
+      if (
+        document.documentElement.hasAttribute("pyxisapp") &&
+        Services.env.exists("PYXIS_DISPLAY_MODE") &&
+        Services.env.get("PYXIS_DISPLAY_MODE") == "fullscreen"
+      ) {
+        window.fullScreen = true;
+      }
+    } catch (e) {
+      console.error("pyxis: fullscreen init failed", e);
+    }
+
+    // PYXIS-DIAG (permanent): the regression guard for "second and subsequent
+    // launches come up with full Firefox chrome".
+    //
+    // This one is deliberately NOT temporary. That bug was reported five
+    // times over two months and misdiagnosed twice, because the only thing
+    // anyone could say about it was what it looked like on a screen no test
+    // can see -- scripts/serial-test.py drives the serial console and QMP
+    // screendump reports "no surface" on Evo's GL scanout. A window that is
+    // born chromeless and has its chrome flags rewritten ~2s later is
+    // invisible to any check made at window open, which is why the earlier
+    // probes (all of which fire at or before load) kept reporting a correct
+    // window. Logging the settled state gives the suites something to assert
+    // on; see scripts/serial-tests/kiosk-relaunch.txt.
+    //
+    // The actual bug was SessionStore.restoreWindowFeatures() reasserting
+    // every WINDOW_HIDEABLE_FEATURES entry as visible -- fixed by the
+    // SessionStore.sys.mjs patch in this series, which reads its rationale.
+    // `toolbarvis` is the load-bearing field: it is the flag SessionStore
+    // flipped, and TabBarVisibility.update() derives the window's whole
+    // popup-like single-tab treatment from it.
+    try {
+      if (document.documentElement.hasAttribute("pyxisapp")) {
+        window.setTimeout(() => {
+          try {
+            let root = document.documentElement;
+            let nav = document.getElementById("nav-bar");
+            let box = document.getElementById("navigator-toolbox");
+            let h = el => (el ? Math.round(el.getBoundingClientRect().height) : -1);
+            console.error(
+              `PYXIS-DIAG chrome-late: app=${root.getAttribute("pyxisapp")} ` +
+                `toolbarvis=${window.toolbar.visible} ` +
+                `navbar=${h(nav)} toolbox=${h(box)} ` +
+                `chromehidden="${root.getAttribute("chromehidden")}"`
+            );
+          } catch (e) {
+            console.error(`PYXIS-DIAG chrome-late: threw: ${e}`);
+          }
+        }, 5000);
+      }
+    } catch (e) {
+      console.error("PYXIS-DIAG chrome-late: install failed", e);
+    }
+
     if (Services.policies.status === Services.policies.ACTIVE) {
       if (!Services.policies.isAllowed("hideShowMenuBar")) {
         document
